  "_comment": [
    "Hardware and site presets, shared by every host. Kinder serves this file verbatim",
    "from its presets route, so its shape is a contract, not an internal detail.",
    "",
    "FULL DESIGN NOTES: docs/presets.md — what a profile may claim, how band overrides",
    "work, and why mu_dark means two different things in this file.",
    "PROVENANCE: validation/provenance.py records where every number below came from,",
    "and a test fails on any value it does not account for.",
    "",
    "Three things an editor has to know before touching anything here:",
    "",
    "1. ORDER IS SIGNIFICANT. The first entry in each catalogue is the default the",
    "   calculator opens on. Kinder serves raw bytes rather than jsonify for this",
    "   reason - Flask would alphabetise the keys and scramble the intended order.",
    "",
    "2. A profile with an 'environment' block is a real site; one without is a hardware",
    "   family and must not gain a location. Inventing one produces wrong airmass and",
    "   moon geometry silently, rather than an error.",
    "",
    "3. A filter's 'telescope' override is keyed by telescope id, and the key matters.",
    "   Unkeyed, a filter measured on one telescope silently applied its number to",
    "   every other. 'castor check' catches a key naming a telescope that does not exist."
